[{"id":2662764086,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6eto42","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** https://github.com/Calinou/godot-sprite3d-vs-meshinstance3d\r\n\r\n<details open>\r\n\r\n<summary>PC specifications</summary>\r\n\r\n- **CPU:** Intel Core i9-13900K\r\n- **GPU:** NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090\r\n- **RAM:** 64 GB (2×32 GB DDR5-5800 C30)\r\n- **SSD:** Solidigm P44 Pro 2 TB\r\n- **OS:** Linux (Fedora 41)\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nUsing an optimized release export template build (`production=yes lto=full`) and the default window size from the testing project.\r\n\r\nAmount | Mesh | Sprite before | Sprite after\r\n-|-|-|-\r\n0 | 8480 FPS (0.12 mspf) | 8480 FPS (0.12 mspf) | 8480 FPS (0.12 mspf)\r\n1,000 | 2896 FPS (0.35 mspf) | 979 FPS (1.02 mspf) | 2790 FPS (0.36 mspf)\r\n5,000 | 762 FPS (1.31 mspf) | 143 FPS (6.99 mspf) | 709 FPS (1.41 mspf)\r\n10,000 | 465 FPS (2.15 mspf) | 64 FPS (15.63 mspf) | 442 FPS (2.26 mspf)\r\n\r\nI also quickly tested the Mobile rendering method and the speedup is more modest there, but MeshInstance3D is already significantly slower than it is in Forward+. From 64 FPS with 10,000 Sprite3Ds, you go to 266 FPS with this PR. For comparison, 10,000 MeshInstance3Ds is 281 FPS. This may be chalked up to the lack of depth prepass in Mobile though, since meshes are opaque in this project (and Sprite3D uses alpha-cut transparency).","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103312#pullrequestreview-2662764086","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103312","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103312#pullrequestreview-2662764086"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103312"}},"submitted_at":"2025-03-06T00:03:25Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2875551657,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6rZW-p","user":{"login":"Ansraer","id":6329420,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjk0MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6329420?u=9b6df29991f0ca8186e28f269b6391ae5dd1bb63&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer","html_url":"https://github.com/Ansraer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ansraer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ok, I took a glance at this PR just now. I like the idea, but am not sure I am happy with the implementation.\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell right now one of the Sprite3Ds (called A for the sake of this discussion) stores the entire mesh and all the other Sprite3Ds that want to use the same mesh access Sprite3D's mesh.\r\n\r\nThis means we have special cases for Sprite3D's sharing their own mesh, accessing another Sprite3D's mesh and what happens when the the Sprite3D that owns the mesh gets deleted (with some kind of handover procedure to let another Sprite3D \"own\" the mesh).\r\n\r\nIMO it would be far simpler if the mesh management was pulled out of Sprite3D entirely (maybe into \"Sprite3DMeshes\"), which would do simple counting for how many Sprite3Ds need a given mesh.\r\nThis way we would remove the seperation between mesh owning and mesh subscribing Sprite3Ds.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103312#pullrequestreview-2875551657","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103312","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103312#pullrequestreview-2875551657"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103312"}},"submitted_at":"2025-05-28T15:28:27Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2907242099,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6tSP5z","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://